        <h1 class="support-title">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <div class="support-subtitle">
            This Privacy Policy explains how DRMA Tech (Delivering Reliable Modern Apps Tech OÜ), the company operating <b>@AppInfo.Title</b> (<a href="@AppInfo.WebSite" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@AppInfo.WebSite</a>), collects, uses, stores, and shares information when you visit or use our website, applications, and related services.
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
            <p><b>Account and authentication information.</b> When you create or use an account, we may process your email address, display name, account identifiers, authentication records, and information provided by your identity provider. Depending on the sign-in method and platform, authentication may be provided through Clerk or Microsoft identity services.</p>
            <p><b>Profile and travel preferences.</b> When you use account features, we may process information you provide about yourself and your travel preferences, such as nationality, passport-issuing country, preferred destinations, interests, lifestyle preferences, and other profile settings used to personalize destination discovery and comparisons.</p>
            <p><b>Saved content and activity.</b> We process information you create, save, or manage through the platform, such as destination wishlists, next-destination lists, travel history, saved destinations, personal notes, comparisons, and preferences. This information allows the platform to provide account-based features and keep your information available across sessions.</p>
            <p><b>Device, technical, and usage information.</b> We and our service providers may collect information such as IP address, approximate location derived from network information, browser and device type, operating system, application version, platform, language, pages visited, interactions, timestamps, and diagnostic or error information. This information helps us operate, secure, troubleshoot, and improve the service.</p>
            <p><b>Communications and feedback.</b> If you contact support, submit feedback, suggest a feature, or participate in an in-platform feedback flow, we process the information and messages you provide, together with relevant account or technical context where available, to respond and improve the platform.</p>
            <p><b>Subscription and transaction information.</b> If you purchase a subscription, we process information needed to manage access and billing, such as the payment provider, product or plan, subscription status, renewal or expiration information, and transaction references. Payment providers process payment details under their own privacy policies.</p>
            <p>You can browse some public destination information without creating an account. Account-based features, including saving personal information and managing travel lists, require authentication.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
            <p>We use information for purposes that include:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Providing and operating the platform, including destination discovery, rankings, comparisons, maps, and destination information.</li>
                <li>Creating and maintaining accounts, authenticating users, and protecting account access.</li>
                <li>Saving and displaying your profile, preferences, wishlists, next-destination lists, travel history, notes, and other account content.</li>
                <li>Personalizing destination suggestions and presenting information relevant to your selected interests, profile, language, and region.</li>
                <li>Managing subscriptions, payments, customer support, and subscription-related communications.</li>
                <li>Responding to questions, feedback, feature suggestions, and privacy requests.</li>
                <li>Understanding how the platform is used, measuring performance, diagnosing errors, and improving features and user experience.</li>
                <li>Displaying, measuring, and protecting advertisements where advertising is enabled.</li>
                <li>Detecting abuse, fraud, security incidents, and activity that may violate our terms or applicable law.</li>
                <li>Complying with legal obligations and establishing, exercising, or defending legal claims.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>3. Legal Bases for Processing</h2>
            <p>Where data protection laws require a legal basis, we process personal information on one or more applicable grounds, depending on the purpose and circumstances:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Contract and requested services:</b> to create and manage your account, provide features you request, save your content, and administer subscriptions.</li>
                <li><b>Legitimate interests:</b> to maintain and secure the platform, prevent abuse, troubleshoot issues, understand service performance, and improve our services, where those interests are not overridden by your rights and freedoms.</li>
                <li><b>Legal obligations:</b> to comply with applicable laws, accounting requirements, lawful requests, and regulatory obligations.</li>
                <li><b>Consent:</b> where required by law or where we choose consent as the applicable basis, including for certain optional cookies, storage technologies, analytics, or advertising activities.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>When we rely on consent, you may withdraw it at any time. Withdrawal does not affect processing that took place before withdrawal. Where we rely on legitimate interests, you may have the right to object, depending on the law that applies to you.</p>
            <p>Some information is necessary to provide account features or services you request. If you do not provide that information, the relevant feature may not be available.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>4. Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>
            <p>Our website and service providers may use cookies, local storage, session storage, scripts, and similar technologies to support essential functionality, remember settings, maintain sessions, understand service usage, diagnose problems, and support advertising.</p>
            <p>These technologies may be operated by us or by third parties, including analytics and advertising providers. They may collect information about your browser, device, interactions with the platform, and advertising activity.</p>
            <p>You can manage or delete cookies through your browser settings. Blocking cookies or browser storage may affect sign-in, preferences, or other features. Browser controls may not affect every technology used by third parties. Where applicable law requires consent or provides an objection or opt-out right for a particular technology, the relevant choice should be provided before or during that processing as required by law.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>5. Analytics, Diagnostics, Feedback, and Advertising</h2>
            <p>Depending on the platform, region, and features enabled, we use third-party services to understand usage, diagnose technical issues, receive feedback, and display advertisements:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Google Analytics</b> helps us understand how visitors use the website and which pages or features are used.</li>
                <li><b>Microsoft Clarity</b> helps us understand how visitors interact with the website, including navigation and page interactions.</li>
                <li><b>Sentry</b> helps us detect errors and diagnose application or service issues.</li>
                <li><b>UserJot</b> allows users to submit feedback and feature suggestions. When you submit feedback while signed in, information associated with your account may be processed to handle the feedback in context.</li>
                <li><b>Google AdSense and Yandex advertising services</b> may display and measure advertisements where enabled. These providers and their partners may use cookies or similar technologies and process device, browser, and advertising-related information to deliver, measure, and protect advertisements. Available advertising controls and the types of advertisements shown may depend on your location, applicable law, and provider settings.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>These providers may process information under their own privacy policies. Their processing is not controlled entirely by us. Please review the relevant provider policies and settings for more information about their practices and available choices.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>6. How We Share Information</h2>
            <p>We do not sell personal information in exchange for money. We disclose information only as reasonably necessary to operate, provide, maintain, secure, and improve the platform, process transactions you request, or comply with legal obligations.</p>
            <p>Depending on the features you use and the platform through which you access the service, information may be shared with these categories of service providers:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><b>Authentication providers:</b> Clerk and Microsoft identity services, which support account registration, sign-in, and authentication.</li>
                <li><b>Hosting, infrastructure, and database providers:</b> Microsoft Azure and Azure Cosmos DB, which support application hosting, backend operations, and data storage.</li>
                <li><b>Analytics and diagnostics providers:</b> Google Analytics, Microsoft Clarity, and Sentry, which help us understand usage and diagnose technical issues.</li>
                <li><b>Feedback providers:</b> UserJot, which supports user feedback and feature suggestions.</li>
                <li><b>Advertising providers:</b> Google AdSense, Yandex advertising services, and their relevant partners, where advertising is enabled.</li>
                <li><b>Payment providers and app stores:</b> Paddle, Stripe, Apple App Store, Google Play, and Microsoft Store, depending on the purchase option offered to you. Not every provider or payment method is available to every user.</li>
                <li><b>Email providers:</b> ZeptoMail, which supports account-related and service-related email communications.</li>
                <li><b>External data, mapping, and content providers:</b> services accessed through RapidAPI, ParseHub, Sherpa, MapTiler, and other sources used to retrieve destination information, data, or map resources. Information such as search terms, destination identifiers, language, or region may be sent when needed to retrieve the information you request.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Some disclosures to analytics or advertising providers may be considered a sale, sharing, or use for targeted or cross-context behavioral advertising under certain privacy laws, even when no money is exchanged. Where applicable, you may have rights to opt out of certain processing. You can contact us using the details in the Contact section to submit a privacy request.</p>
            <p>We may also disclose information when required by law, in response to valid legal process, to protect users or the public, to investigate suspected fraud or security issues, or to establish, exercise, or defend legal claims. If our company is involved in a merger, acquisition, restructuring, or sale of assets, information may be transferred as part of that transaction subject to applicable privacy requirements.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>7. Destination Information and Third-Party Services</h2>
            <p>My Next Spot combines information from public sources and third-party providers to present destination profiles, rankings, statistics, indicators, cost estimates, mobility information, news, weather, maps, and other travel-related information. We may use external APIs, data services, mapping providers, and other sources to retrieve or update this information.</p>
            <p>When you search for or view a destination or related information, relevant search terms, destination identifiers, language, region, or technical request information may be transmitted to the provider supplying that information. The privacy practices of those providers are governed by their own policies.</p>
            <p>Links to accommodation, transportation, government resources, or other external websites may be provided for convenience. We do not operate or control those third-party services and are not responsible for their content, availability, transactions, or privacy practices. Visiting an external service is subject to that provider's terms and privacy policy.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>8. Subscriptions and Payments</h2>
            <p>Subscription plans, prices, billing periods, currencies, and available payment methods may vary by country, device, platform, and current availability. When offered, purchases may be processed by Paddle, Stripe, Apple, Google Play, or Microsoft Store.</p>
            <p>We receive subscription-related information needed to provide the purchased plan and manage access, such as the payment provider, product or plan, subscription status, relevant dates, and transaction references. When payment details are entered directly with a payment provider or app store, we do not receive the full payment card details through that transaction flow. The provider processes payment information under its own privacy policy.</p>
            <p>Deleting your My Next Spot account and cancelling a subscription are separate actions. Account deletion does not automatically cancel an active subscription or stop future charges. You must cancel through the provider or store where you made the purchase. We may retain limited transaction and subscription records for the period required by law or reasonably necessary for accounting, dispute resolution, fraud prevention, and the administration of our services.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>9. Data Retention and Account Deletion</h2>
            <p>We retain personal information for as long as reasonably necessary to provide the platform, maintain your account and saved content, fulfil the purposes described in this Policy, comply with legal obligations, resolve disputes, and protect our services.</p>
            <p>You can request account deletion through the Help Center or by contacting us. We will verify and process your request in accordance with applicable law. After processing, we will delete or anonymize information that we are not required or permitted to retain.</p>
            <p>Some information may be retained for a limited period where necessary to comply with legal or regulatory obligations, maintain accounting and transaction records, prevent fraud, protect security, or establish, exercise, or defend legal claims. Information in backups may remain until the applicable backup cycle is completed and will not be restored for ordinary use except where necessary for recovery or security. Information retained independently by third parties is subject to their own retention policies and obligations.</p>
            <p>You can use the Download Data feature in the Help Center to download certain information associated with your account. The scope and format of available data may depend on the information and features supported by the platform.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>10. Your Privacy Rights and Choices</h2>
            <p>Depending on your location and applicable law, you may have the right to request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal information; receive a copy of certain information; request portability; restrict or object to certain processing; withdraw consent where processing is based on consent; or lodge a complaint with a data protection authority.</p>
            <p>Residents of Brazil may have rights under the LGPD, including confirmation of processing, access, correction, anonymization, blocking or deletion in applicable circumstances, portability subject to regulation, information about sharing, and withdrawal of consent. Residents of the European Economic Area and the United Kingdom may have rights under the GDPR or UK GDPR, including access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, objection, and the right to complain to a supervisory authority. Residents of certain U.S. states may have additional rights under applicable state privacy laws, including rights to know, access, correct, delete, and opt out of certain sales, sharing, or targeted advertising.</p>
            <p>To submit a request, use the Help Center or email <a href="mailto:support@my-next-spot.com">support@my-next-spot.com</a>. We may need to verify your identity or request additional information before processing a request. We will respond within the time required by applicable law. Some requests may be limited by legal exceptions or our need to retain certain information.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>11. Public and Private Content</h2>
            <p>Some destination information and curated content on My Next Spot is public and may be viewed by visitors. Account holders may also save personal information, create lists, maintain travel history, and add notes. Private account content is intended to remain accessible only to you unless you choose to share it through a public link or another sharing feature.</p>
            <p>If you create or share a public list or link, anyone with access to that link may be able to view and further share the content made available through it. Information that you make public may be copied, indexed, or redistributed by others. Review the content and visibility of a list before sharing it, and disable or remove sharing when you no longer want the link to be accessible, where that option is available.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>12. Children's Privacy</h2>
            <p>My Next Spot is intended for a general audience and is not directed to children where their use of the service or the collection of their personal information is prohibited by applicable law. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children in circumstances where parental or guardian consent is required and has not been obtained. If you believe a child has provided us with personal information improperly, please contact us so we can review the matter and take appropriate action.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>13. Security and International Transfers</h2>
            <p>We use reasonable technical and organizational measures designed to protect personal information against unauthorized access, loss, misuse, alteration, or disclosure. These measures may include access controls, secure communications, and safeguards provided by our infrastructure and service providers. No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
            <p>DRMA Tech is established in Estonia. Our service providers may process information in the European Economic Area, the United States, Brazil, and other countries where they or their infrastructure operate. Where required by applicable law, international transfers are made using an appropriate transfer mechanism and safeguards.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>14. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
            <p>We may update this Privacy Policy to reflect changes to My Next Spot, our features, service providers, or applicable legal requirements. The latest version will be published on this page with its updated date. Where required, we will provide additional notice of material changes.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-section">
            <h2>15. Contact</h2>
            <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or want to exercise your privacy rights, contact us at <a href="mailto:support@my-next-spot.com">support@my-next-spot.com</a> or use the <a href=@($"/{Culture}/help")>Help Center</a>.</p>
            <p>My Next Spot is operated by DRMA Tech (Delivering Reliable Modern Apps Tech OÜ). For general company inquiries, contact <a href="mailto:contact@drma-tech.com">contact@drma-tech.com</a>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="support-footer">
            <p>Last updated: November 11, 2026</p>
